From: Harvi654 <202698022+Harvi654@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] server: Keep an integrity level per token.

AI-assisted (Claude), original code; LGPL-2.1-or-later. Not submitted upstream.

On Windows 10 a process started from a normal console runs with the
limited half of the administrator's split token and reports Medium
integrity (S-1-16-8192); from an elevated console it reports High
(S-1-16-12288). The native .NET Framework COM shim reads the process
token's integrity level and, at High, ignores COM classes registered
only in HKCU\Software\Classes, so per-user .NET classes fail to load
(measured with a VBScript CreateObject in both consoles).

Wine has no integrity level in the token: ntdll reports High for every
token. Store one in the server's token: Medium for a limited token, High
for a full or default admin token, copied by duplication (impersonation,
restricted and primary duplicates), and return it in get_token_info.
The linked token is created with the opposite elevation type and gets
its level from that.

The token object's own mandatory label (the SACL returned for
LABEL_SECURITY_INFORMATION) is a separate thing on Windows and is left
as it was: token_create_admin still assigns a High label, and changing
it is a separate question for the measurement. Setting the level
(NtSetInformationToken) stays a stub. Access checks do not enforce
mandatory labels in Wine, so the lower level changes no access.

v1 2026-11-24: first version, expected values from the console
measurements; MEASURE of the derived tokens pending.

v2 2026-11-25: no code change. MEASURE on Windows 10 (normal and
elevated console, x86_64 and i686) confirmed the level of every derived
token; L1, paired L2 and the Inventor, Nastran and AutoCAD L4 passed.
Promoted to the series for winum-11.22-3.

v3 (2026-11-27): Rebased to Wine 11.23, context only, logic unchanged.
Regenerate the protocol headers and tracing from protocol.def with make_requests (988 to 989).

